  "tours": [
    {
      "id": "tour:execution",
      "title": "How Cobra selects and runs a command",
      "summary": "Cobra finds the selected command and normally parses its flags; apps can disable parsing to pass raw arguments to handlers. Help requests and commands without a runnable handler print help and return. Runnable commands check arguments, run pre-run hooks, check flag rules, and call the handler; successful handlers continue through post-run hooks. Version printing and completion requests are outside this tour.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "view": "view:execution",
          "focus": [
            "execution:1"
          ],
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "command.go",
              "symbol": "Command.ExecuteC",
              "span": {
                "from": 35,
                "to": 40
              },
              "role": "usage"
            },
            {
              "file": "command.go",
              "symbol": "Command.Find",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "note": "### Command selection follows the command tree\n\nBy default, `Find` walks subcommand names after removing flags. With `TraverseChildren`, `Traverse` parses each parent’s flags while descending.",
          "editor": {
            "primary": "command.go"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t2",
          "view": "view:execution",
          "focus": [
            "execution:2"
          ],
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "command.go",
              "symbol": "Command.ExecuteC",
              "span": {
                "from": 58,
                "to": 64
              },
              "role": "usage"
            }
          ],
          "note": "### The selected command receives the remaining input\n\nSelection ends with a command and its remaining flag strings. Cobra then runs that command, so child commands use their own handlers and validation.",
          "editor": {
            "primary": "command.go"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t3",
          "view": "view:execution",
          "focus": [
            "execution:3"
          ],
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "command.go",
              "symbol": "Command.ParseFlags",
              "span": {
                "from": 1,
                "to": 1
              },
              "role": "usage"
            },
            {
              "file": "command.go",
              "symbol": "Command.execute",
              "span": {
                "from": 11,
                "to": 16
              },
              "role": "usage"
            }
          ],
          "note": "### Flag parsing can be skipped by the app\n\nCobra initializes help and, when configured, version flags at execution time. With `DisableFlagParsing`, the handler receives raw arguments; otherwise a parse error stops the command.",
          "editor": {
            "primary": "command.go"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t4",
          "view": "view:execution",
          "focus": [
            "execution:4"
